[2026-03-15T07:14:42.841Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018GkWdUapHhZ45EjL2YQHFR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nSet up your API key by visiting https://app.replay.io settings, creating an API key, and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings for viewing\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check CLI and browser versions\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps`** - Upload source maps for debugging\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nRecord a session at a specific URL, then upload it when complete. The tool will prompt you to upload after recording ends, or you can manually upload using the recording ID.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05a60624-77ab-43db-a283-e7b7bde69626","uuid":"ec4d2dde-142e-4b7f-95df-f6a3ac6b0927","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nSet up your API key by visiting https://app.replay.io settings, creating an API key, and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings for viewing\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check CLI and browser versions\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps`** - Upload source maps for debugging\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nRecord a session at a specific URL, then upload it when complete. The tool will prompt you to upload after recording ends, or you can manually upload using the recording ID.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options.","durationMs":3556,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T07:14:43.249Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rs6RPeh7yKV32TkkcmLbiA","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As summarized in the documentation:\n\n\"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings. These recordings perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe tool organizes around two main investigation approaches:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened through dependency tracking and state inspection.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe document recommends a structured approach: frame your investigation as a question, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools for context, develop a hypothesis supported by data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Notable Features\n\n- **Points**: Discrete execution moments with potential state changes\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of specific execution points\n- **Logpoint tool**: Particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution cycles to identify unexpected behavior\n\nThe documentation emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and instead following evidence systematically through the recorded data."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05a60624-77ab-43db-a283-e7b7bde69626","uuid":"45658611-62fd-45c8-9f42-d6e7762f5d26","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As summarized in the documentation:\n\n\"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings. These recordings perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe tool organizes around two main investigation approaches:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened through dependency tracking and state inspection.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe document recommends a structured approach: frame your investigation as a question, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools for context, develop a hypothesis supported by data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Notable Features\n\n- **Points**: Discrete execution moments with potential state changes\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of specific execution points\n- **Logpoint tool**: Particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution cycles to identify unexpected behavior\n\nThe documentation emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and instead following evidence systematically through the recorded data.","durationMs":3449,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
