[2026-03-15T07:26:12.217Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GP8t9tpJmwmL648k8eNCf4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Overview\n     2→\n     3→This repository is a platform for agentic app building. You will build and/or maintain one or more\n     4→web apps according to a set of skills and guidelines which will evolve as you get better at building apps.\n     5→\n     6→Key directories:\n     7→\n     8→* `apps`: Has one subdirectory for each app that has been built or has been specified and still needs to be built.\n     9→* `skills/messages`: Skills for responding to messages from the user (e.g. bug reports, log analysis).\n    10→* `skills/tasks`: Skills for performing tasks. See `skills/AGENTS.md` for details.\n    11→* `reports`: Final generated reports from log analysis (see `skills/review/`).\n    12→* `report-data`: Intermediate analysis data used during report generation.\n    13→* `tasks`: The task queue (`tasks-<containerName>.json`) managed by scripts in `scripts/`.\n    14→* `logs`: Log files from work that has been performed. `worker-current.log` is the log for\n    15→  the work currently being done.\n    16→\n    17→You are running within a container and can run test suites for applications and connect to various\n    18→external services using instructions in the relevant skill files.\n    19→\n    20→**CRITICAL — FIRST THING YOU DO when responding to a user message:**\n    21→\n    22→1. **BEFORE doing ANY work**, list the files in `skills/messages/` and read any skill\n    23→   whose name matches the user's request.\n    24→2. If a matching skill exists, follow it exactly.\n    25→3. Only if no matching skill exists should you proceed on your own — and then write a new\n    26→   skill document in `skills/messages/` afterward so you handle it correctly next time.\n    27→\n    28→Do NOT run git commands, search code, or take any other action until you have checked for a\n    29→matching skill. This is the highest-priority rule when handling user messages.\n    30→\n    31→Do NOT modify this AGENTS.md file unless the user explicitly instructs you to.\n    32→All domain-specific guidance belongs in skill files under `skills/`.\n    33→\n    34→## Worker Execution\n    35→\n    36→The worker processes tasks from `tasks/tasks-<containerName>.json` sequentially. For each task,\n    37→it passes all subtasks to Claude as a single prompt and checks for a `<DONE>` signal.\n    38→\n    39→- If `<DONE>` is signaled: the task is dequeued and the worker moves to the next task.\n    40→- If `<DONE>` is NOT signaled: the task is retried (up to 3 times before being skipped).\n    41→\n    42→The worker commits changes after each task automatically. Focus on completing the\n    43→subtasks — do not worry about committing or exiting.\n    44→\n    45→When you have completed ALL subtasks in your task, output `<DONE>` to signal completion.\n    46→\n    47→## Task System\n    48→\n    49→Work is managed through a JSON task queue at `tasks/tasks-<containerName>.json`. The file contains an object\n    50→with a `tasks` array. Each task has a `skill`, an array of `subtasks` (description strings),\n    51→a `timestamp`, and an optional `app` name:\n    52→\n    53→```json\n    54→{\n    55→  \"tasks\": [\n    56→    {\n    57→      \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/maintain/checkDirectives.md\",\n    58→      \"subtasks\": [\n    59→        \"CheckTestSpecAuth: Check testSpec.md directive violations in Authentication\",\n    60→        \"CheckComponentsAuth: Check writeApp.md directive violations in Authentication\",\n    61→        \"CheckTestsAuth: Check writeTests.md directive violations in Authentication\"\n    62→      ],\n    63→      \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-20T00:00:00.000Z\",\n    64→      \"app\": \"sales-crm\"\n    65→    }\n    66→  ]\n    67→}\n    68→```\n    69→\n    70→The agent NEVER reads or writes task files directly. Instead, use `add-task` via stdin heredoc:\n    71→\n    72→```bash\n    73→npx tsx /repo/scripts/add-task.ts <<'EOF'\n    74→[\n    75→  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/build/writeApp.md\", \"app\": \"SalesCRM\", \"subtasks\": [\"SetupApp: Setup the app\", \"DesignDatabase: Design the database\"] },\n    76→  { \"skill\": \"skills/tasks/build/writeTests.md\", \"app\": \"SalesCRM\", \"subtasks\": [\"WriteTestAuth: Write test for Auth\"] }\n    77→]\n    78→EOF\n    79→```\n    80→\n    81→Tasks are inserted at the front of the queue in the order listed (first element = first to run).\n    82→Each task object must have `skill` and `subtasks`. `app` is optional.\n    83→\n    84→**CRITICAL: `add-task` usage rules**\n    85→\n    86→- When unpacking tasks, put ALL new tasks in a **single `add-task` call**. Do NOT call\n    87→  `add-task` multiple times.\n    88→- Write out every task explicitly in the JSON array. Do NOT use loops, scripts, or code\n    89→  to generate tasks programmatically.\n    90→- All subtasks in a task share the same skill. Group related subtasks together — for example,\n    91→  all checks for a single page go in one task.\n    92→- When a skill needs to \"unpack\" into sub-tasks, use `add-task` to insert them at the\n    93→  front of the queue.\n    94→\n    95→**CRITICAL: Task scope rules**\n    96→\n    97→- You MUST only work on subtasks that were assigned to you in your current prompt. Your assigned\n    98→  subtasks are the ones passed to you by the worker — nothing else.\n    99→- When you add new tasks via `add-task`, you MUST NOT start working on those tasks.\n   100→  They will be picked up by a future worker iteration.\n   101→- If you have completed all of your assigned subtasks and the only remaining work is tasks you\n   102→  added to the queue, you are DONE. Commit your changes and output `<DONE>` immediately.\n   103→  Do NOT continue working on the newly queued tasks.\n   104→- Adding tasks to the queue is NOT the same as doing those tasks. Add them and stop.\n   105→\n   106→## Tech Stack\n   107→\n   108→- **Vite** for build tooling\n   109→- **TypeScript** for all source code (strict mode)\n   110→- **React 18** for UI (single-page application)\n   111→- **Redux** for client side state management\n   112→- **shadcn/ui** for components\n   113→- **Neon** for database backend (Postgres).\n   114→- **Netlify Functions** for any backend/serverless functions. Place functions in `netlify/functions/`. Use `netlify dev` for local development.\n   115→- **File Storage** use UploadThing with the provided token for any file storage.\n   116→\n   117→## Database\n   118→\n   119→All database accesses must happen in backend Netlify functions. Netlify functions should be focused\n   120→and operate on specific parts of the database corresponding to the needs of one or more specific\n   121→frontend components.\n   122→\n   123→## Running Tests\n   124→\n   125→You MUST read `skills/tasks/build/testing.md` and precisely follow its instructions when running\n   126→tests and debugging test failures.\n   127→\n   128→## Quality Gates\n   129→\n   130→Before each commit, run `npm run check` (see `skills/scripts/check.md`). Do not commit\n   131→code that fails typecheck or lint.\n   132→\n   133→## Commits\n   134→\n   135→The worker commits automatically after each iteration. Do not commit manually unless\n   136→explicitly asked to by a skill or prompt.\n   137→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jtoz8nRnGt1Jnb56xzcV9q","session_id":"05a60624-77ab-43db-a283-e7b7bde69626","uuid":"2f297d7a-efe5-4b9b-a777-8ebbf5b7dec4"}
