n `boundingBox()` returns coordinates below the viewport, `page.mouse.move()` dispatches events at those viewport coordinates where no element actually exists. The solution is to scroll the element into view before attempting to drag it. The price slider works fine with Playwright's mouse events, so it's not a general React pointer event issue. Let me compare the two sliders more carefully—the price slider has a much larger range (13785) compared to the duration slider (90), and both handles are visible on the page. I'm trying to trace through the calculation logic to see where the duration slider might be failing when the mouse moves to a specific percentage of the track.\n\nActually, I'm wondering if the real problem is that the element might be scrolled out of view, which could cause `boundingBox()` to return coordinates outside the viewport range, and then `page.mouse.move()` wouldn't work correctly since it expects viewport coordinates.\n\nThe solution is to scroll the slider handle into view before attempting to drag it. I need to update the `dragSliderHandle` helper function to call `scrollIntoView()` on the track element first, ensuring the handle is visible in the viewport before we try to interact with it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":109699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":858,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05a60624-77ab-43db-a283-e7b7bde69626","uuid":"7de81beb-0e1d-4f69-b5de-2af2bee04b72"}
